odd-claude is a port to Claude Code of the ODD harness distributed as
gentle-shell (upstream, MIT License). Behaviour, semantics and the design of
the doctor/status commands are derived from that project. All upstream
copyright and permission notices remain those of their authors.

Ported skills (Apache License, Version 2.0)
-------------------------------------------
The following skills under skills/ are adapted from the upstream skills
distributed with that project, which are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). They keep the
`license: Apache-2.0` frontmatter field. The original text and ideas were
written by the upstream authors; odd-claude changed the tool names, paths and
naming for Claude Code and set `metadata.author` to odd-claude.

  - branch-pr
  - chained-pr
  - cognitive-doc-design
  - comment-writer
  - issue-creation
  - judgment-day
  - skill-creator
  - skill-improver
  - ui-design
  - work-unit-commits

Changes are made without warranty; the Apache-2.0 text applies to those files
only as stated above. The tui-design skill is original text with its own
attribution in skills/tui-design/NOTICE.md.

Ported review agents and chain (MIT License)
--------------------------------------------
The agents odd-review-risk, odd-review-resilience, odd-review-readability and
odd-review-reliability and the skill 4r-review are adapted from the upstream
review lens agents and the 4R review chain (MIT License, same project as
above). odd-claude removed the upstream review tools and lineage machinery,
passes the candidate change in the prompt, and restricts the agents to
Read, Grep and Glob. The checklists, severity scale and finding format keep
the upstream wording where possible.

Ported themes (MIT License)
---------------------------
The color palettes of themes/odd.json, odd-cute.json and odd-bold.json are converted from the upstream Pi themes of the same project (MIT License), mapped to Claude Code theme tokens.
